    "created_at": "2022-07-03T08:50:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-03T08:50:48Z",
    "body": "So, the error is due to the limiting case when all elements of `weights = list(map(int, np.random.randint(1, n_items, size=n_items)))` have the same value, because then you end up having `np.random.randint(n,n)` in line 490 which, rightly so, crashes.\r\n\r\nI think we did not see this bug because tests always had `n_items` relatively large.\r\n\r\nLet us check on Monday what's the appropriate value for the `weight_capacity` in this limiting case.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
